From 830819bc74d0846e75262798542b4accf2b5a331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip DiSarro <philipdisarro@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:43:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add CIP-153 Value builtins
 (insertCoin/lookupCoin/unionValue/valueContains/valueData/unValueData)

DefaultFun entries with flat tags 94-99 and uni tag 13 (both verified
against plutus-core Default/Builtins.hs and Default/Universe.hs), a
Const.Value carrier modeled on PlutusCore.Value.toList (nested sorted
association list, normalized: strictly ascending keys, no zero
quantities, no empty inner maps), denotations in PlutusCore/Value/Basic
matching plutus-core Value.hs line by line (key-length and signed
128-bit quantity validation, insertCoin amount-0 delete without
validation, unionValue overflow error and exact-zero drop,
valueContains negative-amount errors, unValueData shape/ordering/bounds
validation), CEK dispatch, flat decoding of value constants
(pack-normalized, K/Quantity validation as in the Flat instances), cost
model arms from builtinCostModel{A,B,C}.json with ValueTotalSize /
ValueMaxDepth / DataNodeCount size measures, and a test suite: unit
tests per builtin plus an end-to-end gate importing the compiled
wsc-poc Programmable Logic Global validator (PV11, uses all six
builtins) and running it on the CEK machine.
